        136
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bedroom and bathroom are upstairs, and the only toilet is upstairs.",
      "cites": [
        133
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "There is a rail on the right side of the stairs when going up.",
      "cites": [
        140
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Margaret Doyle goes up the stairs one at a time, holding on with her right hand.",
      "cites": [
        141
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "When coming down the stairs, the rail is on the wrong side for her right hand, so she goes down sideways or on her bottom if tired.",
      "cites": [
        143
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Margaret Doyle sometimes goes down the stairs on her bottom, especially when tired, and says it is safer and done in private.",
      "cites": [
        145
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "There is only one frame, which is left at the bottom and used by holding onto the wall upstairs.",
      "cites": [
        147
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Margaret Doyle would like a second rail and a second frame for the upstairs stairs.",
      "cites": [
        152
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "There are several rugs in the hall and in the living room, which were Frank's mother's or brought back from a holiday in Wales.",
      "cites": [
        154
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "The rugs are a trip hazard, especially with a frame.",
      "cites": [
        156
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kevin has repeatedly told Margaret Doyle about the rugs being a hazard.",
      "cites": [
        157
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Margaret Doyle gets up in the night to use the toilet once or twice.",
      "cites": [
        160
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Margaret Doyle now leaves the landing light on at night to help with nighttime toilet use.",
      "cites": [
        161
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bathroom is only a few steps from the bedroom.",
      "cites": [
        163
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Margaret Doyle does not currently have a pendant alarm or a fall-detecting button on her person.",
      "cites": [
        165
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Margaret Doyle said she does not want to wear a necklace or look like an 'old woman'.",
      "cites": [
        166
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Margaret Doyle expressed interest in a wrist-worn fall-detecting device that can call for help automatically.",
      "cites": [
        171
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Margaret Doyle said a fall-detecting device might have been useful on March 3rd, when she fell and lay there for two hours.",
      "cites": [
        172
      ],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    }
  ]
